-- erwartet: C001
-- **667 -- `walk … levels` over a COMPOUND constant expression, and the fence stays here.**
--
-- On 2026-09-03 `walk_` learned to read a `const` NAME: `levels EBENEN` with
-- `const EBENEN : u32 = 4` had drawn *"`walk … levels` that is not a number"* over a
-- declaration that says `4`. The value was never guessed and never computed twice -- it
-- stands in `Namen::konstwert`, folded by `umgebung.rs` before the emitter starts, and the
-- `static` array length plus `feldlaenge_von` had been reading it for days. **`walk_` held
-- the weaker of two registers over one thing** (W7), and `messung/fragmente/F09.gab` paid
-- for it with an emitter refusal.
--
-- WHY THIS FILE, AND WHY IT IS NOT THE SAME REPAIR ONE DOOR FURTHER
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------
-- A repair that reads a NAME does not read `EBENEN + 1`, and the difference is not a
-- rounding error in the implementation -- it is where the read stops being a read. The
-- constant table holds one entry per `const` ITEM; a compound expression at the use site is
-- a second evaluator wherever it is folded, and building one inside the emitter is exactly
-- the move the W7 note above forbids.
--
-- So the fence stands at the bare name, and this file is the fence-post. **The checker says
-- nothing** -- `4 items, 0 errors, 0 hints` -- and the emitter refuses BY NAME, which is the
-- one behaviour a generator owes at a form it cannot lower: *it refuses instead of emitting
-- something plausible.*
--
-- > **And it falls in the useful direction.** The day `umgebung.rs` folds use-site
-- > expressions and the emitter reads THAT answer, this probe goes red and asks to be
-- > withdrawn -- the same shape `beispiele/gift/653`-`657` took when `at port` learned to
-- > lower. *A refusal without a measured defect is not a rule* (Rule A, second half).
--
-- The control is `messung/fragmente/F09.gab` itself: `levels EBENEN` and
-- `node : [Pte; EINTRAEGE]` lower since the same day, and `beispiele/07-eintritt-und-boot.gab`
-- keeps the literal form green.

module gift::walklevels {

const EBENEN : u32 = 4;

format Pte endian little {
    praesent : bool @0,
    rahmen   : u64 embeds [63:1] scale 2,
}

-- `EBENEN` alone lowers. `EBENEN + 1` is one step past the constant table.
walk T levels EBENEN + 1 {
    node : [Pte; 512],
    down : rahmen when it.praesent,
    leaf : it.praesent,
}

}
